module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartBasicOpenLocalization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartDiagram
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Etale.LocalizationAcrossSquareZero

/-!
# The arrows of the chart diagram over a basic open are open immersions

Let `0 ⟶ ℐ ⟶ 𝒜 ⟶ 𝒪_X ⟶ 0` be a square-zero extension of the structure sheaf of an algebraic
space `X` over `Y`, in the sense of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension`, and let
`h : U ⟶ V` be a morphism of the small étale site of `X` between objects with affine underlying
scheme.  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.etale_chartSpec_map_of_isAffine` says that
`Spec(𝒜(U)) ⟶ Spec(𝒜(V))` is then étale.  This file upgrades that to an **open immersion** when
`U` is a basic open of `V`, i.e. when `𝒪_X(U)` is the localization of `𝒪_X(V)` away from a
section — which is the case of the chart diagram of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT] that the gluing of
the charts uses.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`: **the kernel ideal
  of the reduction over `U` is generated by the image of the kernel ideal over `V`.**  This is
  the identity `K_V · 𝒜(U) = K_U` of the proof of the source, read off from the base-change
  statement `…isBaseChange_ker_app_of_isAffine`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine`: **the
  sections of `𝒜` over `U` are the localization of its sections over `V` away from any lift of
  the section defining `U` as a basic open of `V`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_of_isAffine`:
  **consequently `Spec(𝒜(U)) ⟶ Spec(𝒜(V))` is an open immersion.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.contains_chartSpec_obj_of_isAffine`: **and
  `Spec(𝒜(U))` is again an object of the big fppf site** as soon as `Spec(𝒜(V))` is — the
  cutoff bookkeeping, propagated along the localization.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension`
  `.isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_openChartInclusion_basicOpen`: **the open immersion with no
  hypothesis beyond affineness of the larger chart**, the localization being the one supplied by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalization_away_chartRing_openChart_basicOpen`.

## Implementation notes

The ring-theoretic content is `Stacks.Etale.isLocalization_away_of_squareZero`: an algebra which
is formally smooth over a square-zero extension and whose reduction is a localization away from
an element is itself a localization away from a lift of that element.  Formal smoothness comes
from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine`, the square-zero
condition from `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_pow_two_eq_bot`, and the identity
between the kernel ideals from `…ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`; the last step from the
localization to the open immersion is Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.of_isLocalization`.

**Why the localization hypothesis is a hypothesis.**  Being a basic open is a property of the
pair `U ⊆ V` of charts that the small étale site does not record: an object of the site is an
arbitrary étale scheme over `X`, and the statement `𝒪_X(U) = 𝒪_X(V)[1/s]` is exactly what
singles out the inclusions along which the charts of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT] are glued.  The
three statements therefore carry it, and
`…isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_openChartInclusion_basicOpen` discharges it for the basic opens
of an affine chart, where it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalization_away_chartRing_openChart_basicOpen`.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.**  This is one step of the proof of Tag 05ZT — that the diagram
`U ↦ Spec(𝒜(U))` has open immersions for its arrows over the basic opens of the affine charts,
which is what makes it a gluing datum.  Nothing here constructs the ambient algebraic space or
identifies its structure sheaf, and no declaration quantifies over more than a single pair of
charts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05ZT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01LH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01LH), the gluing of schemes
  over a basis of the topology of the base, whose datum these open immersions feed.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

namespace SquareZeroExtension

variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {f : X ⟶ Y} (E : SquareZeroExtension B S hS f)

/-- **The kernel ideal of the reduction over an affine chart is generated by the image of the
kernel ideal over any affine chart it maps to.**

This is the identity `K_V · 𝒜(U) = K_U` used in the proof of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT] — the
inclusion that is not formal.  It is read off from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isBaseChange_ker_app_of_isAffine` by the induction
principle `CategoryTheory.IsBaseChange.inductionOn` of a base change: every element of `K_U` is a
sum of `𝒜(U)`-multiples of images of elements of `K_V`. -/
theorem ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom) :
    RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom ≤
      Ideal.map (algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)))
        (RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom) := by
  let g : RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom →ₗ[E.A.obj.obj (op V)]
      RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom :=
    { toFun := fun x => ⟨algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))
        (x : E.A.obj.obj (op V)), by
          rw [RingHom.mem_ker, halg, SquareZeroExtension.π_app_map_apply, RingHom.mem_ker.mp x.2,
            map_zero]⟩
      map_add' := fun x y => Subtype.ext (map_add
        (algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))) _ _)
      map_smul' := fun a x => Subtype.ext (by
        change algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))
            (a * (x : E.A.obj.obj (op V))) =
          a • algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) (x : E.A.obj.obj (op V))
        rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul]) }
  have hbc := SquareZeroExtension.isBaseChange_ker_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg g
    (fun _ => rfl)
  have key : ∀ n : RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom,
      (n : E.A.obj.obj (op U)) ∈ Ideal.map
        (algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)))
        (RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom) := by
    intro n
    induction n using hbc.inductionOn with
    | tmul m =>
      change algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) (m : E.A.obj.obj (op V)) ∈ _
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ m.2
    | smul s n ih =>
      change s * (n : E.A.obj.obj (op U)) ∈ _
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ s ih
    | add n₁ n₂ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      change (n₁ : E.A.obj.obj (op U)) + (n₂ : E.A.obj.obj (op U)) ∈ _
      exact Ideal.add_mem _ ih₁ ih₂
  intro z hz
  exact key ⟨z, hz⟩

/-- **Over affine charts the sections of `𝒜` on a basic open are a localization.**  If the
sections of `𝒪_X` over `U` are the localization of its sections over `V` away from the reduction
of some `a : 𝒜(V)`, then the sections of `𝒜` over `U` are the localization of `𝒜(V)` away from
`a` itself.

This is `Stacks.Etale.isLocalization_away_of_squareZero` with every hypothesis discharged: the
reductions are surjective over affine charts by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine`, the kernel of the
reduction over `V` has square zero by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_pow_two_eq_bot`, the kernel over `U` is
generated by its image by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`, and `𝒜(U)` is
formally smooth over `𝒜(V)` because it is étale, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine`. -/
theorem isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom)
    [Algebra ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halgO : algebraMap ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
        ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))
      = ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.map h.op).hom)
    (a : E.A.obj.obj (op V))
    [IsLocalization.Away ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))] :
    IsLocalization.Away a (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) := by
  have : Algebra.Etale (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) :=
    SquareZeroExtension.algebraEtale_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg
  refine Stacks.Etale.isLocalization_away_of_squareZero
    (E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom
    (SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E V hV)
    (SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E U hU) (fun x => ?_)
    (SquareZeroExtension.ker_pow_two_eq_bot B S hS E (op V))
    (SquareZeroExtension.ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg) a
  rw [halg, halgO]
  exact SquareZeroExtension.π_app_map_apply B S hS E h x

/-- **The arrow of the chart diagram over a basic open of an affine chart is an open
immersion.**  If the sections of `𝒪_X` over `U` are the localization of its sections over `V`
away from the reduction of some `a : 𝒜(V)`, then `Spec(𝒜(U)) ⟶ Spec(𝒜(V))` is an open immersion.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine` read
through `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.of_isLocalization`.  It is the arrow of the gluing
datum of [Stacks Project, Tag 01LH] out of which the proof of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT] builds
the ambient space of the realizing thickening. -/
theorem isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom)
    [Algebra ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halgO : algebraMap ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
        ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))
      = ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.map h.op).hom)
    (a : E.A.obj.obj (op V))
    [IsLocalization.Away ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))] :
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion ((chartSpec B S hS E).map h) := by
  have : IsLocalization.Away a (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) :=
    SquareZeroExtension.isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg halgO a
  have hmap : CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))) = E.A.obj.map h.op := by
    rw [halg]
    exact CommRingCat.ofHom_hom _
  have hoi := _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.of_isLocalization
    (R := E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (S := E.A.obj.obj (op U)) a
  rw [hmap] at hoi
  exact hoi

/-- **The chart of the diagram over a basic open stays inside the site.**  If
`Spec(𝒜(V))` is an object of the big fppf site, so is `Spec(𝒜(U))` whenever `U` is a basic open
of `V` in the sense of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine`: the sections
of `𝒜` over `U` are then a localization of its sections over `V`, and a spectrum of a
localization of an object's ring of functions is again an object, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_Spec_lt_of_isLocalization`.

This is the cutoff bookkeeping that the gluing of the charts owes: an object of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite` is a scheme whose size is below the cutoff, so every chart of the
diagram has to be shown small before it can be a chart of an algebraic space.  Note that it is
*propagation* only — it says nothing about the base chart `Spec(𝒜(V))`, whose size is not bounded
by the datum of a square-zero extension at all, the module `ℐ` being an arbitrary quasi-coherent
module. -/
theorem contains_chartSpec_obj_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom)
    [Algebra ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halgO : algebraMap ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
        ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))
      = ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.map h.op).hom)
    (a : E.A.obj.obj (op V))
    [IsLocalization.Away ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op U))]
    (hVsite : B.Contains ((chartSpec B S hS E).obj V)) :
    B.Contains ((chartSpec B S hS E).obj U) := by
  have : IsLocalization.Away a (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) :=
    SquareZeroExtension.isLocalization_away_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg halgO a
  exact _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_Spec_lt_of_isLocalization B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
    B.cutoff_isStrongPrelimit (Submonoid.powers a) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) hVsite

/-- **Unconditionally: the arrow of the chart diagram over a basic open of an affine chart is an
open immersion.**  For an affine chart `V` and a section `a` of `𝒜` over it, the basic open of
the reduction of `a` is again an affine chart, and `Spec(𝒜)` of the inclusion is an open
immersion.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_of_isAffine`
with its localization hypothesis discharged by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocalization_away_chartRing_openChart_basicOpen`, and the affineness of
the smaller chart by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAffine_chartScheme_openChart_basicOpen`. -/
theorem isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_openChartInclusion_basicOpen (V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    (a : E.A.obj.obj (op V)) :
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion ((chartSpec B S hS E).map
      (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 V
        (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
          ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
            ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)))) := by
  have hU := isAffine_chartScheme_openChart_basicOpen B S hS X.1 V hV
    ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
  let _ : Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V))
      (E.A.obj.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 V
        (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
          ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
            ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a))))) :=
    (E.A.obj.map (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 V
      (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
          ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a))).op).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj (op V))
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj
        (op (openChart B S hS X.1 V
          (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
            ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
              ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a))))) :=
    ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.map (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 V
      (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
        ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
          ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a))).op).hom.toAlgebra
  have hloc : IsLocalization.Away ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.obj
        (op (openChart B S hS X.1 V
          (((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj
            ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)).basicOpen
              ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a))))) :=
    isLocalization_away_chartRing_openChart_basicOpen B S hS X.2 V hV
      ((E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom a)
  exact SquareZeroExtension.isOpenImmersion_chartSpec_map_of_isAffine B S hS E _ hU hV
    (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _) (RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra _) a

end SquareZeroExtension

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
